        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Standard laminate is not waterproof, and the best laminate is waterproof only from the top for a limited window. That still makes it a good floor for most of the house, including kitchens, as long as spills are wiped up, the perimeter is sealed in wet rooms and slow leaks are caught early with a few cheap alarms.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Where water can sit unnoticed or arrive all at once, in full bathrooms, laundry rooms and basements with any history of water, choose vinyl plank or tile instead. If laminate is the right call for your rooms, our <a href="/best-laminate-flooring/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-semibold hover:underline">best laminate flooring</a> picks note which lines carry real surface-water ratings and what their warranties actually cover.
          </p>
